{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"similar-operose-alligator","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe duration probe can measure end-to-end close wall time and the verifier workflow, but it currently labels the large interval before the completion verdict as an inferred residual. That attribution is insufficient: a recent normal close was silent for roughly eight minutes, and existing cohorts have much larger gaps. Minimal direct instrumentation is approved only if it cannot exacerbate the performance problem.\n\n## Performance constraint\nInstrumentation must use only `time.monotonic_ns()`, integer arithmetic, and cheap dictionary assignments on the existing call path. It must add no event, tracker write, commit/push, file read, Git command, network call, tracing backend, worker, lock, retry, sleep, or model call. The values must piggyback on the existing `COMPLETION_VERDICT.metrics` payload and its existing sidecar write. Prove the bookkeeping overhead with a local standard-library microbenchmark and record the result before landing.\n\n## Plan\n- Start one timing dictionary at the close-tail entry and thread it through the existing `close_ticket → _completion_precheck → _check_work_landed → commit_impact.referencing_commits` call chain using optional arguments so other callers retain current behavior.\n- Record direct milliseconds for `pre_verifier_total_ms`, `structural_scan_ms`, `material_policy_ms`, `descendant_scope_ms`, `landing_check_ms`, `verifier_call_ms`, `git_history_read_ms`, `alias_index_build_ms`, `ticket_ref_resolution_ms`, and `diff_validation_ms`.\n- Record direct workload counts for commits inspected, distinct ticket references, descendant ids in scope, and referencing commits found.\n- Merge these fields into the verdict metrics immediately after the existing verifier call, before the existing PASS/FAIL sidecar emit. Preserve the verifier metrics already attached by gate dispatch.\n- Update the reusable duration probe to read the direct fields. Report older records as `legacy_uninstrumented`; never give an unexplained residual a causal operation name.\n- Add synthetic RED-first tests for timing propagation, workload counts, preservation of existing verifier metrics, legacy probe labeling, and the no-extra-observer-work contract.\n\n## Timing boundaries\n- `structural_scan_ms`: existing open-child/newly-unblocked batch scan.\n- `material_policy_ms`: existing plan-review close currency/material recheck.\n- `descendant_scope_ms`: canonical-id resolution plus transitive descendant collection/resolution.\n- `landing_check_ms`: existing work-landed and file-impact policy checks.\n- `verifier_call_ms`: existing bounded completion-verifier/auto-resume call.\n- `pre_verifier_total_ms`: close-tail entry through the instant immediately before that verifier call.\n- Nested history/index/reference/diff fields partition directly observed work inside the landing check; they are not inferred.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A model-backed PASS and FAIL `COMPLETION_VERDICT` carries all ten direct timing fields without losing existing consumption metrics.\n- [ ] Sidecar workload counts include commits inspected, distinct references, descendant ids, and referencing commits found.\n- [ ] Instrumentation adds no I/O, subprocess, network, tracker event/write, lock, retry, background work, or model call.\n- [ ] Existing callers of commit-impact and close-precheck helpers remain behavior-compatible when no timing dictionary is supplied.\n- [ ] The duration probe uses direct fields when present and labels older rows `legacy_uninstrumented`, with no causal label on inferred residuals.\n- [ ] Synthetic tests fail on current main and pass after the implementation.\n- [ ] A standard-library microbenchmark demonstrates negligible bookkeeping overhead and its command/result are recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] Focused tests, import walk, lint, typecheck, and the default non-integration/non-external test suite pass.\n- [ ] No agent-duration guidance is changed; documented ranges still require explicit user confirmation after a post-instrumentation cohort.","id":"3f22-7fd4-aae7-48b4","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["performance","completion-gate","observability","metrics"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Emit direct gated-close phase timings in the completion sidecar"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787543174004595001,"uuid":"19ae3301-183c-4813-8c72-048f3d916833"}